# Event24 Web App — Agent Workflow

## Before coding

1. Read `.agent` fully.
2. Inspect existing implementation before adding a new file/component.
3. Check Module Inventory.
4. Check whether the screen still uses mock data or real Laravel data.
5. Verify any non-public API endpoint against the current Laravel contract.
6. Preserve the existing Lovable visual language.

## Architecture rules

This project is Vite + React.

Do NOT introduce:

- Next.js
- server actions
- /api/proxy
- HMAC signatures
- X-API-Signature
- X-API-Timestamp
- API secrets in Vite
- Supabase

## API

All Laravel API requests use the centralized API clients.

Every API request must send X-API-Key.

Participant requests may also send the participant_token Bearer token.

Organizer requests may also send the organizer_token Bearer token.

Never mix those tokens.

Never call raw axios/fetch from a page/component when the central API/service architecture can be used.

## UI

The surviving Lovable application is the visual/theme source.

Reuse existing UI before building replacements.

Do not downgrade polished UI into generic forms/cards during backend integration.

Mobile behavior must remain intact.

## Before finishing

1. Update `.agent`.
2. Update living sections, not only Change Log.
3. List files changed.
4. Record API contracts confirmed or changed.
5. Record mock → real-data transitions.
6. Verify TypeScript/build.
7. Work is incomplete until `.agent` matches reality.
